concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5 Interpretation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-5 ;
    values:originalText "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears: ACC means the Australian Crime Commission. ACC Act means the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002. access, in relation to a stored communication, has the meaning given by section 6AA. This definition does not apply to Schedule 1. accessible, in relation to a communication, has the meaning given by section 5H. access request has the meaning given by subsection 107P(1). ACMA means the Australian Communications and Media Authority. activities prejudicial to security has the same meaning as it has in the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979. affidavit includes affirmation. AFP employee has the same meaning as in the Australian Federal Police Act 1979. AFP Minister has the meaning given by section 100.1 of the Criminal Code. agency means:  (a) except in Chapter 2—an interception agency or another enforcement agency; or  (b) in Chapter 2—an interception agency.  Chapter 1  Introduction" ;
    skos:definition "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears: ACC means the Australian Crime Commission. ACC Act means the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002. access, in relation to a stored communication, has the meaning given by section 6AA. This definition does not apply to Schedule 1. accessible, in relation to a communication, has the meaning given by section 5H. access request has the meaning given by subsection 107P(1). ACMA means the Australian Communications and Media Authority. activities prejudicial to security has the same meaning as it has in the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979. affidavit includes affirmation. AFP employee has the same meaning as in the Australian Federal Police Act 1979. AFP Minister has the meaning given by section 100.1 of the Criminal Code. agency means:  (a) except in Chapter 2—an interception agency or another enforcement agency; or  (b) in Chapter 2—an interception agency.  Chapter 1  Introduction"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d980e40cc283b5bd025ef98d4f603e502b91457deb6f4b81285653e5f5f6289c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definitions and explanations of terms used in the Act." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.19" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5-norm .
