doc:sec-5aa a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "5AA Eligible Commonwealth authority declarations" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The Minister may, by notice published in the Gazette, declare a Commonwealth Royal Commission to be an eligible Commonwealth authority for the purposes of this Act if the Minister is satisfied that the Royal Commission is likely to inquire into matters that may involve the commission of a prescribed offence." ;
    cof:pageNumber "72"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5ab a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5AB Authorised officers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-5ab ;
    values:originalText "Authorised officers of an enforcement agency  (1) The head (however described) of an enforcement agency may, by writing, authorise a management office or management position in the enforcement agency for the purposes of subparagraph (b)(iii) of the definition of authorised officer in subsection 5(1).  Introduction  Chapter 1 Interpretation  Part 1-2  Section 5AC  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Authorised officers of the Australian Federal Police  (1A) The Commissioner of Police may authorise, in writing, a senior executive AFP employee who is a member of the Australian Federal Police to be an authorised officer.  (2) A copy of an authorisation must be given to the Communications Access Coordinator:  (a) in the case of an authorisation made under subsection (1)— by the head of the enforcement agency; and  (b) in the case of an authorisation made under subsection (1A)— by the Commissioner of Police. Authorisations are not legislative instruments  (3) An authorisation made under this section is not a legislative instrument." ;
    skos:definition "Authorised officers of an enforcement agency  (1) The head (however described) of an enforcement agency may, by writing, authorise a management office or management position in the enforcement agency for the purposes of subparagraph (b)(iii) of the definition of authorised officer in subsection 5(1).  Introduction  Chapter 1 Interpretation  Part 1-2  Section 5AC  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Authorised officers of the Australian Federal Police  (1A) The Commissioner of Police may authorise, in writing, a senior executive AFP employee who is a member of the Australian Federal Police to be an authorised officer.  (2) A copy of an authorisation must be given to the Communications Access Coordinator:  (a) in the case of an authorisation made under subsection (1)— by the head of the enforcement agency; and  (b) in the case of an authorisation made under subsection (1A)— by the Commissioner of Police. Authorisations are not legislative instruments  (3) An authorisation made under this section is not a legislative instrument."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fcc88bbafad3a5fb5ceb649b22e6206a70ca4a0a6ec1a01c5fb350f99b58effd" ;
    cof:pageNumber "72"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5ab-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5ab-ss-1a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5ab-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5ab-ss-3 ;
