    cof:title "5E(1) Serious contraventions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a serious contravention is a contravention of a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory that:  (a) is a serious offence; or  (b) is an offence punishable:  (i) by imprisonment for a period, or a maximum period, of at least 3 years; or  (ii) if the offence is committed by an individual—by a fine, or a maximum fine, of at least 180 penalty units; or  (iii) if the offence cannot be committed by an individual— by a fine, or a maximum fine, of at least 900 penalty units; or  Introduction  Chapter 1 Interpretation  Part 1-2  Section 5F  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) could, if established, render the person committing the contravention liable:  (i) if the contravention were committed by an individual— to pay a pecuniary penalty of 180 penalty units or more, or to pay an amount that is the monetary equivalent of 180 penalty units or more; or  (ii) if the contravention cannot be committed by an individual—to pay a pecuniary penalty of 900 penalty units or more, or to pay an amount that is the monetary equivalent of 900 penalty units or more." ;
    cof:pageNumber "88"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5e-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5E(2) Serious contraventions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-5e-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a contravention, or a contravention of a particular kind, is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to be a contravention, or to be a contravention of that kind, as the case may be, that:  (a) has been committed or is being committed; or  (b) is suspected on reasonable grounds of having been committed, of being committed or of being likely to be committed." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a contravention, or a contravention of a particular kind, is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to be a contravention, or to be a contravention of that kind, as the case may be, that:  (a) has been committed or is being committed; or  (b) is suspected on reasonable grounds of having been committed, of being committed or of being likely to be committed."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "32ad76634182b6ff75597a0a6913b6c787af75f39f74555ec0bd45d5e8fbcab6" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5e ;
    cof:pageNumber "88"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A contravention is taken to be a contravention if it has been committed or is suspected on reasonable grounds of having been committed." ;
