doc:sec-5e-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "5E(2) Serious contraventions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a contravention, or a contravention of a particular kind, is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to be a contravention, or to be a contravention of that kind, as the case may be, that:  (a) has been committed or is being committed; or  (b) is suspected on reasonable grounds of having been committed, of being committed or of being likely to be committed." ;
