concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5e-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5E(3) Serious contraventions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-5e-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) To avoid doubt, a reference in this section to a number of penalty units in relation to a contravention of a law of a State or a Territory includes a reference to an amount of a fine or pecuniary penalty that is equivalent, under section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914, to that number of penalty units. 5F  When a communication is passing over a telecommunications system  For the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1), a communication:  (a) is taken to start passing over a telecommunications system when it is sent or transmitted by the person sending the communication; and  (b) is taken to continue to pass over the system until it becomes accessible to the intended recipient of the communication.  Chapter 1  Introduction" ;
    skos:definition "(3) To avoid doubt, a reference in this section to a number of penalty units in relation to a contravention of a law of a State or a Territory includes a reference to an amount of a fine or pecuniary penalty that is equivalent, under section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914, to that number of penalty units. 5F  When a communication is passing over a telecommunications system  For the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1), a communication:  (a) is taken to start passing over a telecommunications system when it is sent or transmitted by the person sending the communication; and  (b) is taken to continue to pass over the system until it becomes accessible to the intended recipient of the communication.  Chapter 1  Introduction"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "268a36e6b37b08990b150f14171de005a245e7e68d70c66bf508834460033d9e" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5e ;
    cof:pageNumber "88"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Reference to penalty units includes reference to equivalent fine or pecuniary penalty amount." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
