concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6da a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6DA Nominated ART members"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-6da ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, nominate a person who holds one of the following appointments to the Administrative Review Tribunal to issue warrants (except to the National Anti-Corruption Commission) under Part 2-5:  (a) Deputy President;  (b) senior member;  (c) general member.  (2) Despite subsection (1), the Attorney-General must not nominate a person who holds an appointment as a senior member on a  Introduction  Chapter 1 Interpretation  Part 1-2  Section 6DB  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  sessional basis or a general member of the Tribunal unless the person:  (a) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of another federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State or of the Australian Capital Territory; and  (b) has been so enrolled for not less than 5 years.  (3) A nomination ceases to have effect if:  (a) the nominated ART member ceases to hold an appointment of a kind set out in subsection (1); or  (b) the Attorney-General, by writing, withdraws the nomination.  (4) A nominated ART member has, in performing a function of or connected with, issuing a warrant under Part 2-5, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, nominate a person who holds one of the following appointments to the Administrative Review Tribunal to issue warrants (except to the National Anti-Corruption Commission) under Part 2-5:  (a) Deputy President;  (b) senior member;  (c) general member.  (2) Despite subsection (1), the Attorney-General must not nominate a person who holds an appointment as a senior member on a  Introduction  Chapter 1 Interpretation  Part 1-2  Section 6DB  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  sessional basis or a general member of the Tribunal unless the person:  (a) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of another federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State or of the Australian Capital Territory; and  (b) has been so enrolled for not less than 5 years.  (3) A nomination ceases to have effect if:  (a) the nominated ART member ceases to hold an appointment of a kind set out in subsection (1); or  (b) the Attorney-General, by writing, withdraws the nomination.  (4) A nominated ART member has, in performing a function of or connected with, issuing a warrant under Part 2-5, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e0523ada5cbdce84515cb7fb2aafc592344fa7310cd9c0d9e61586bb60fd9f67" ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6da-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6da-ss-2 ;
