doc:sec-6g-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "6G(3) Officer of the Commonwealth, of a State or of a Territory" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) A reference in this Act to an officer of a Territory includes a reference to:  (a) a person holding, or acting in, an office (including a judicial office) or appointment, or employed, under a law of the Territory; and  (b) a person who is, or is a member of, an authority or body established for a public purpose by or under a law of the Territory, or is an officer or employee of such an authority or body.  Introduction  Chapter 1 Interpretation  Part 1-2  Section 6H  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "102"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6h a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6H Person to whom application relates"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-6h ;
    values:originalText "For the purposes of this Act, an application by an agency to a Judge or nominated ART member for a warrant relates to a particular person if, and only if, information has been, or is proposed to be, given to the Judge or nominated ART member under Part 2-5, in connection with the application, in order to satisfy the Judge or nominated ART member, in relation to the person, of the matters referred to in:  (a) in the case of a warrant under section 48—paragraphs 46(1)(c) and (d), 46(4)(c), (d) and (e), 46(7)(c) to (h), 46(9)(c), (d) and (e), or 46(12)(c) to (g), as the case requires; or  (b) in the case of any other Part 2-5 warrant—paragraphs 46(1)(c) and (d), 46(4)(c), (d) and (e), 46(7)(c) to (h), 46A(1)(c) and (d), 46A(2A)(c), (d) and (e), 46A(2C)(c) to (h), 46A(2E)(c), (d) and (e), or 46A(2G)(a) to (g), as the case requires; or  (c) in the case of a stored communications warrant— subparagraph 116(1)(d)(i) or (ii), as the case requires." ;
    skos:definition "For the purposes of this Act, an application by an agency to a Judge or nominated ART member for a warrant relates to a particular person if, and only if, information has been, or is proposed to be, given to the Judge or nominated ART member under Part 2-5, in connection with the application, in order to satisfy the Judge or nominated ART member, in relation to the person, of the matters referred to in:  (a) in the case of a warrant under section 48—paragraphs 46(1)(c) and (d), 46(4)(c), (d) and (e), 46(7)(c) to (h), 46(9)(c), (d) and (e), or 46(12)(c) to (g), as the case requires; or  (b) in the case of any other Part 2-5 warrant—paragraphs 46(1)(c) and (d), 46(4)(c), (d) and (e), 46(7)(c) to (h), 46A(1)(c) and (d), 46A(2A)(c), (d) and (e), 46A(2C)(c) to (h), 46A(2E)(c), (d) and (e), or 46A(2G)(a) to (g), as the case requires; or  (c) in the case of a stored communications warrant— subparagraph 116(1)(d)(i) or (ii), as the case requires."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3b3660e3ea43c31c39fc2b94c1eaa498aad23f6082a4d4c57e7c7fbf76b8f8d4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "103"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Information must be provided to satisfy the Judge or nominated ART member about a particular person." ;
    dc:description "true" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
