concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6n a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6N Declaration of staff members of State Police Forces"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-6n ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies to an agency that is the Police Force of a State.  (2) The Minister may make a written declaration that members of an agency included in a specified class of members of the agency occupy positions corresponding to those of AFP employees who are not members of the Australian Federal Police.  (3) Members included in the class of members of an agency specified in a declaration are referred to in this Act, in relation to the agency concerned, as staff members." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies to an agency that is the Police Force of a State.  (2) The Minister may make a written declaration that members of an agency included in a specified class of members of the agency occupy positions corresponding to those of AFP employees who are not members of the Australian Federal Police.  (3) Members included in the class of members of an agency specified in a declaration are referred to in this Act, in relation to the agency concerned, as staff members."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6aa7ecfcab95f6542f6959270f5c8cd12357b0b5b7efe2e61bbcaab472c9dcba" ;
