concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-10-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10(2) Issue of warrant by Director-General of Security in emergency"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Where a warrant under this section authorizes entry on premises, the warrant shall state whether entry is authorized to be made at any time of the day or night or only during specified hours and may, if the Director-General of Security thinks fit, provide that entry may be made without permission first being sought or demand first being made, and authorize measures that he or she is satisfied are necessary for that purpose." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Where a warrant under this section authorizes entry on premises, the warrant shall state whether entry is authorized to be made at any time of the day or night or only during specified hours and may, if the Director-General of Security thinks fit, provide that entry may be made without permission first being sought or demand first being made, and authorize measures that he or she is satisfied are necessary for that purpose."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "19e2e58e82a647d1e09f6cfdccbf1a63838f56d82e949d91a458696f119fa389" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-10 ;
    cof:pageNumber "124"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorization for entry without permission or demand" ;
    dc:description "entry may be made without permission first being sought or demand first being made" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
