concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-4a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31A(4A) Attorney-General may authorise interception for developing"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-31a-ss-4a ;
    values:originalText "(4A) If paragraph (1)(a) applies to the authorisation, this Part does not require that an authorised interception must involve:  (a) one or more employees of the security authority referred to in that paragraph; and  (b) one or more employees of a carrier referred to in that paragraph; acting together or in the presence of each other." ;
    skos:definition "(4A) If paragraph (1)(a) applies to the authorisation, this Part does not require that an authorised interception must involve:  (a) one or more employees of the security authority referred to in that paragraph; and  (b) one or more employees of a carrier referred to in that paragraph; acting together or in the presence of each other."@en ;
