concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-4b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31A(4B) Attorney-General may authorise interception for developing"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-31a-ss-4b ;
    values:originalText "(4B) To avoid doubt, subparagraph (2)(a)(ii) has the effect that lawfully intercepted information obtained under the authorisation may be communicated, used or recorded for the purposes of development or testing of technologies, or interception capabilities." ;
    skos:definition "(4B) To avoid doubt, subparagraph (2)(a)(ii) has the effect that lawfully intercepted information obtained under the authorisation may be communicated, used or recorded for the purposes of development or testing of technologies, or interception capabilities."@en ;
