concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31A(1) Attorney-General may authorise interception for developing"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-31a-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) the Attorney-General gives a section 31A authorisation in response to an application made by:  (i) the head (however described) of a security authority; or  (ii) a person acting as that head; and  (b) the authorisation covers the employees of a carrier;  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications" ;
