concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31B Authorisation of employees of a security authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-31b ;
    values:originalText "(1) The following persons:  (a) the head (however described) of a security authority;  (b) an officer of the security authority covered by an approval in force under subsection (2); may, by writing, authorise employees of the authority for the purposes of this Part.  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Authorisation of interception for developing and testing interception capabilities  Part 2-4  Section 31C  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) The head (however described) of a security authority may, by writing, approve an officer of the authority for the purposes of paragraph (1)(b)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The following persons:  (a) the head (however described) of a security authority;  (b) an officer of the security authority covered by an approval in force under subsection (2); may, by writing, authorise employees of the authority for the purposes of this Part.  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Authorisation of interception for developing and testing interception capabilities  Part 2-4  Section 31C  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) The head (however described) of a security authority may, by writing, approve an officer of the authority for the purposes of paragraph (1)(b)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3eccee1ec3ffab5a8456ced068fa62e34fac02ae49755ea1bfb0c509f0c6e8d5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "148"^^xsd:integer ;
