concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-37 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "37 Revocation of declaration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-37 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If requested by the Premier of a State to revoke a declaration in force under section 34 in relation to an eligible authority of that State, the Minister shall, by notice in writing published in the Gazette, revoke the declaration.  (2) Subject to subsection (1), the Minister may, by notice in writing published in the Gazette, revoke a declaration in force under section 34 in relation to an eligible authority of a State if, and only if, the Minister is satisfied that:  (a) the law of that State no longer makes satisfactory provision in relation to the authority as mentioned in subsection 35(1);  (b) the extent of compliance with a requirement of a law of that State, being a requirement of a kind referred to in subsection 35(1), has been unsatisfactory in so far as the requirement relates to the authority;  (c) no agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being an agreement entered into by that State that relates to the authority, is in force;  (d) the extent of compliance by that State with the terms of an agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Warrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5 Declaration of State Law Enforcement Authorities as Agencies  Division 2  Section 38  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  an agreement entered into by that State, has been unsatisfactory in so far as the agreement relates to the authority; or  (e) the extent of compliance by the chief officer of the authority, or by officers of the authority, with this Act has been unsatisfactory." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If requested by the Premier of a State to revoke a declaration in force under section 34 in relation to an eligible authority of that State, the Minister shall, by notice in writing published in the Gazette, revoke the declaration.  (2) Subject to subsection (1), the Minister may, by notice in writing published in the Gazette, revoke a declaration in force under section 34 in relation to an eligible authority of a State if, and only if, the Minister is satisfied that:  (a) the law of that State no longer makes satisfactory provision in relation to the authority as mentioned in subsection 35(1);  (b) the extent of compliance with a requirement of a law of that State, being a requirement of a kind referred to in subsection 35(1), has been unsatisfactory in so far as the requirement relates to the authority;  (c) no agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being an agreement entered into by that State that relates to the authority, is in force;  (d) the extent of compliance by that State with the terms of an agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Warrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5 Declaration of State Law Enforcement Authorities as Agencies  Division 2  Section 38  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  an agreement entered into by that State, has been unsatisfactory in so far as the agreement relates to the authority; or  (e) the extent of compliance by the chief officer of the authority, or by officers of the authority, with this Act has been unsatisfactory."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "296fc50da203e199e1e5d66ee930053091b3f7067f53097bfc629f8a3c63105a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "154"^^xsd:integer ;
