    values:originalText "(2) Subject to subsection (1), the Minister may, by notice in writing published in the Gazette, revoke a declaration in force under section 34 in relation to an eligible authority of a State if, and only if, the Minister is satisfied that:  (a) the law of that State no longer makes satisfactory provision in relation to the authority as mentioned in subsection 35(1);  (b) the extent of compliance with a requirement of a law of that State, being a requirement of a kind referred to in subsection 35(1), has been unsatisfactory in so far as the requirement relates to the authority;  (c) no agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being an agreement entered into by that State that relates to the authority, is in force;  (d) the extent of compliance by that State with the terms of an agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Warrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5 Declaration of State Law Enforcement Authorities as Agencies  Division 2  Section 38  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  an agreement entered into by that State, has been unsatisfactory in so far as the agreement relates to the authority; or  (e) the extent of compliance by the chief officer of the authority, or by officers of the authority, with this Act has been unsatisfactory." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Subject to subsection (1), the Minister may, by notice in writing published in the Gazette, revoke a declaration in force under section 34 in relation to an eligible authority of a State if, and only if, the Minister is satisfied that:  (a) the law of that State no longer makes satisfactory provision in relation to the authority as mentioned in subsection 35(1);  (b) the extent of compliance with a requirement of a law of that State, being a requirement of a kind referred to in subsection 35(1), has been unsatisfactory in so far as the requirement relates to the authority;  (c) no agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being an agreement entered into by that State that relates to the authority, is in force;  (d) the extent of compliance by that State with the terms of an agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Warrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5 Declaration of State Law Enforcement Authorities as Agencies  Division 2  Section 38  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  an agreement entered into by that State, has been unsatisfactory in so far as the agreement relates to the authority; or  (e) the extent of compliance by the chief officer of the authority, or by officers of the authority, with this Act has been unsatisfactory."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "14ab229e9fb45a2c4b322257082c34fc46626f131b4a09e73edf959661d3e24d" ;
