doc:sec-42-ss-4a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "42(4A) Affidavit to accompany written application" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4A) If the application is for a named person warrant, the affidavit must set out:  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Warrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5 Applications for warrants  Division 3  Section 43  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) the name or names by which the person is known; and  (b) details (to the extent these are known to the chief officer) sufficient to identify the telecommunications services the person is using, or is likely to use; and  (ba) if the warrant would authorise interception of communications made by means of a telecommunications device or telecommunications devices identified in the warrant—details (to the extent these are known to the chief officer) sufficient to identify the telecommunications device or telecommunications devices that the person is using, or is likely to use; and  (c) the number of previous applications (if any) for warrants that the agency has made and that related to the person or to a service that the person has used; and  (d) the number of warrants (if any) previously issued on such applications; and  (e) particulars of the use made by the agency of information obtained by interceptions under such warrants." ;
    cof:pageNumber "162"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-42-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42(5) Affidavit to accompany written application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Notwithstanding subsection (1), a written application may be accompanied by 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, but for this subsection, this section would have required an affidavit accompanying the application to set out, specify or state." ;
    skos:definition "(5) Notwithstanding subsection (1), a written application may be accompanied by 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, but for this subsection, this section would have required an affidavit accompanying the application to set out, specify or state."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ae6d5ebf536c2572c3b0f92e454f885bc796d33b44ffb5c198dad745c67626a9" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-42 ;
    cof:pageNumber "162"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Allows multiple affidavits with written application" ;
