doc:sec-45-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45(1) Application by interception agency of Queensland" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if an interception agency of Queensland applies, under section 39, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART member for a warrant in respect of a telecommunications service or a person. PIM may make submissions" ;
    cof:pageNumber "165"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-45-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "45(2) Application by interception agency of Queensland"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-45-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to the Judge or nominated ART member about the following matters:  (a) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a telecommunications service—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 46(2)(a) to (f), 46(5)(a) to (gb), 46(8)(a) to (e), 46(10)(a) to (h) or 46(13)(a) to (e), as the case requires;  (b) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a person—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 46A(2)(a) to (f), 46A(2B)(a) to (gb), 46A(2D)(a) to (e), 46A(2F)(a) to (h) or 46A(2H)(a) to (e), as the case requires.  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications" ;
    skos:definition "(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to the Judge or nominated ART member about the following matters:  (a) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a telecommunications service—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 46(2)(a) to (f), 46(5)(a) to (gb), 46(8)(a) to (e), 46(10)(a) to (h) or 46(13)(a) to (e), as the case requires;  (b) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a person—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 46A(2)(a) to (f), 46A(2B)(a) to (gb), 46A(2D)(a) to (e), 46A(2F)(a) to (h) or 46A(2H)(a) to (e), as the case requires.  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bdccdf88d9effa7ecd637fd99295a88990e0874cd80081f5e91432b004193bfa" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-45 ;
