doc:sec-45-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45(2) Application by interception agency of Queensland" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to the Judge or nominated ART member about the following matters:  (a) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a telecommunications service—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 46(2)(a) to (f), 46(5)(a) to (gb), 46(8)(a) to (e), 46(10)(a) to (h) or 46(13)(a) to (e), as the case requires;  (b) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a person—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 46A(2)(a) to (f), 46A(2B)(a) to (gb), 46A(2D)(a) to (e), 46A(2F)(a) to (h) or 46A(2H)(a) to (e), as the case requires.  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications" ;
    cof:pageNumber "165"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-45a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "45A State law not affected"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-45a ;
    values:originalText "If:  (a) a person (the applicant) applies, or proposes to apply, under section 39, on behalf of an interception agency of Victoria or Queensland for a warrant in respect of a telecommunications service or a person; and  (b) a law of that State authorises or requires the applicant:  (i) to notify the PIM of that State of the application or proposed application; or  (ii) to notify the PIM of that State of any information that relates to the application or proposed application; or  (iii) to give the PIM of that State any document that relates to the application or proposed application; then nothing in this Act prevents the applicant from making the notification or giving the document to the PIM of that State.  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Warrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5 Warrants  Division 4  Section 46  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "If:  (a) a person (the applicant) applies, or proposes to apply, under section 39, on behalf of an interception agency of Victoria or Queensland for a warrant in respect of a telecommunications service or a person; and  (b) a law of that State authorises or requires the applicant:  (i) to notify the PIM of that State of the application or proposed application; or  (ii) to notify the PIM of that State of any information that relates to the application or proposed application; or  (iii) to give the PIM of that State any document that relates to the application or proposed application; then nothing in this Act prevents the applicant from making the notification or giving the document to the PIM of that State.  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Warrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5 Warrants  Division 4  Section 46  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "806e91e4d193c523b4cc5f2d404388742c44d79685c31dcb813f1d6f6efe664a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "166"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Notification requirements for interception agencies" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.166" ;
