doc:sec-49-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "49(6) Form and content of warrant" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) In subsection (5), warrant means a warrant issued under this Act." ;
    cof:pageNumber "194"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49-ss-6a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "49(6A) Form and content of warrant"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-49-ss-6a ;
    values:originalText "(6A) To avoid doubt, a warrant issued on the basis that a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force remains in force for the period mentioned in subsection (3) even if the order ceases to be in force, provided that the order is replaced by a succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order. Note 1: If there is no succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, the warrant must be revoked (see section 57). Note 2: A control order is not a succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to an extended supervision order, and vice versa (see section 6U)." ;
    skos:definition "(6A) To avoid doubt, a warrant issued on the basis that a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force remains in force for the period mentioned in subsection (3) even if the order ceases to be in force, provided that the order is replaced by a succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order. Note 1: If there is no succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, the warrant must be revoked (see section 57). Note 2: A control order is not a succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to an extended supervision order, and vice versa (see section 6U)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8058c52e5aeb25b283926655b2bcde8b895397840413148119c5df9dfab73ea7" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49 ;
    cof:pageNumber "194"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Warrant remains in force despite changes to supervisory order." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
