concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-50 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "50 Issue of warrant on telephone application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-50 ;
    values:originalText "(1) As soon as practicable after completing and signing a warrant issued on a telephone application, a Judge or nominated ART member shall:  (b) inform the person who made the application on the agency’s behalf of:  (i) the terms of the warrant; and  (ii) the day on which, and the time at which, the warrant was signed; and  (c) give the warrant to that person.  (2) A Judge or nominated ART member who issues a warrant on a telephone application shall keep a copy of the warrant." ;
    skos:definition "(1) As soon as practicable after completing and signing a warrant issued on a telephone application, a Judge or nominated ART member shall:  (b) inform the person who made the application on the agency’s behalf of:  (i) the terms of the warrant; and  (ii) the day on which, and the time at which, the warrant was signed; and  (c) give the warrant to that person.  (2) A Judge or nominated ART member who issues a warrant on a telephone application shall keep a copy of the warrant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d7a515e410daf95226ad5fcc5ac7a33bb0d6b829178d4e9f734d1021fe721c87" ;
    cof:pageNumber "197"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-50-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-50-ss-2 ;
