    values:originalText "(2) A Judge or nominated ART member who issues a warrant on a telephone application shall keep a copy of the warrant." ;
    cof:pageNumber "197"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-51 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "51 Action by agency after warrant issued on telephone application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-51 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (in this section called the applicant) who makes a telephone application on an agency’s behalf shall comply with this section within one day after the day on which a warrant is issued on the application.  (2) The applicant shall cause each person who gave information to the Judge or nominated ART member in connection with the application to swear an affidavit setting out the information so given by the person.  (3) The applicant shall give to the Judge or nominated ART member:  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person (in this section called the applicant) who makes a telephone application on an agency’s behalf shall comply with this section within one day after the day on which a warrant is issued on the application.  (2) The applicant shall cause each person who gave information to the Judge or nominated ART member in connection with the application to swear an affidavit setting out the information so given by the person.  (3) The applicant shall give to the Judge or nominated ART member:  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"@en ;
