    cof:title "52(3) Judge or nominated ART member may revoke warrant where" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If:  (a) a warrant has been issued to an agency; and  (b) another agency or the Organisation is exercising authority under that warrant (see section 55); and  (c) the warrant is revoked under subsection (1); the chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued must:  (d) immediately inform the chief officer of the other agency or the Director-General of Security (as the case requires) of the revocation; and  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Warrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5 Warrants  Division 4  Section 54  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (e) give a copy of the instrument of revocation to the person referred to in paragraph (d) as soon as practicable." ;
    cof:pageNumber "198"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-54 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "54 Entry into force of warrants"@en ;
