concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-59b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59B Notification to Ombudsman or Inspector-General of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-59b ;
    values:originalText "Intelligence and Security in relation to Part 5.3 warrants  (1) Within 6 months after a Part 5.3 warrant is issued in response to an application by a Commonwealth agency, the chief officer of the agency must:  (a) if the agency is the ACC:  (i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security that the warrant has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security a copy of the warrant; and  (b) otherwise:  (i) notify the Ombudsman that the warrant has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the warrant.  (2) As soon as practicable after an officer of the agency contravenes any of the following conditions, restrictions or provisions, the chief  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Warrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5 Warrants  Division 4  Section 59C  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  officer of the agency must notify the Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security (as the case requires) of the contravention:  (a) a condition or restriction specified in the warrant under subsection 49(2);  (b) the following provisions, to the extent that they apply to the warrant:  (i) paragraph 57(1)(b);  (ii) subsection 63(1);  (iii) subsection 63(2);  (iv) section 79;  (c) section 79AA;  (d) subsection 103B(4).  (3) A failure to comply with subsection (1) or (2) does not affect the validity of the warrant." ;
    skos:definition "Intelligence and Security in relation to Part 5.3 warrants  (1) Within 6 months after a Part 5.3 warrant is issued in response to an application by a Commonwealth agency, the chief officer of the agency must:  (a) if the agency is the ACC:  (i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security that the warrant has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security a copy of the warrant; and  (b) otherwise:  (i) notify the Ombudsman that the warrant has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the warrant.  (2) As soon as practicable after an officer of the agency contravenes any of the following conditions, restrictions or provisions, the chief  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Warrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5 Warrants  Division 4  Section 59C  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  officer of the agency must notify the Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security (as the case requires) of the contravention:  (a) a condition or restriction specified in the warrant under subsection 49(2);  (b) the following provisions, to the extent that they apply to the warrant:  (i) paragraph 57(1)(b);  (ii) subsection 63(1);  (iii) subsection 63(2);  (iv) section 79;  (c) section 79AA;  (d) subsection 103B(4).  (3) A failure to comply with subsection (1) or (2) does not affect the validity of the warrant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f847cdfa93359bfcf84f3dea47b020f4091fc5464a588a3a67c5b36d88af31a4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "202"^^xsd:integer ;
