concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-59c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59C Notification to Ombudsman or Inspector-General of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-59c ;
    values:originalText "Intelligence and Security in relation to Part 9.10 warrants  (1) Within 6 months after a Part 9.10 warrant is issued in response to an application by a Commonwealth agency, the chief officer of the agency must:  (a) if the agency is the ACC:  (i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security that the warrant has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security a copy of the warrant; and  (b) otherwise:  (i) notify the Ombudsman that the warrant has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the warrant.  (2) As soon as practicable after an officer of the agency contravenes any of the following conditions, restrictions or provisions, the chief officer of the agency must notify the Ombudsman or the  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications" ;
    skos:definition "Intelligence and Security in relation to Part 9.10 warrants  (1) Within 6 months after a Part 9.10 warrant is issued in response to an application by a Commonwealth agency, the chief officer of the agency must:  (a) if the agency is the ACC:  (i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security that the warrant has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security a copy of the warrant; and  (b) otherwise:  (i) notify the Ombudsman that the warrant has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the warrant.  (2) As soon as practicable after an officer of the agency contravenes any of the following conditions, restrictions or provisions, the chief officer of the agency must notify the Ombudsman or the  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9dd05c108a3dae76e28fd9d89df15a596abbbcd6f47cdc815872722b271b8234" ;
    cof:pageNumber "203"^^xsd:integer ;
