    skos:definition "(1) A person may:  (a) for a purpose connected with a proceeding begun before the commencement of this Part, or for 2 or more such purposes, and for no other purpose, communicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of; or  (b) give in evidence in such a proceeding; information:  (c) obtained by intercepting a communication before that commencement, whether or not in contravention of subsection 7(1); or  (d) obtained, before that commencement, by virtue of a warrant issued under section 11A."@en ;
