concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-64a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "64A Dealing in connection with Inspector-General’s functions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-64a ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person may, in connection with an IGIS official exercising a power, or performing a function or duty, as an IGIS official, communicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of, the following:  (a) information obtained by intercepting a communication passing over a telecommunications system (whether or not that information is lawfully intercepted information);  (b) interception warrant information.  (2) This section applies despite any other provision of this Part.  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person may, in connection with an IGIS official exercising a power, or performing a function or duty, as an IGIS official, communicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of, the following:  (a) information obtained by intercepting a communication passing over a telecommunications system (whether or not that information is lawfully intercepted information);  (b) interception warrant information.  (2) This section applies despite any other provision of this Part.  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"@en ;
