concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "65(2) Dealing in information obtained by Organisation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-65-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been communicated under subsection (1) may, in the proper performance or exercise of the person’s functions, duties or powers:  (a) for the purposes (if any) approved, and subject to the conditions (if any) specified, by the Attorney-General in writing:  (i) communicate that information to another person (the second person); and  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Dealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6  Section 65  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (ii) use that information; and  (c) make a record of that information; and the second person, and any other person to whom that information is communicated under this subsection may communicate it to another person, and use and make a record of it." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been communicated under subsection (1) may, in the proper performance or exercise of the person’s functions, duties or powers:  (a) for the purposes (if any) approved, and subject to the conditions (if any) specified, by the Attorney-General in writing:  (i) communicate that information to another person (the second person); and  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Dealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6  Section 65  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (ii) use that information; and  (c) make a record of that information; and the second person, and any other person to whom that information is communicated under this subsection may communicate it to another person, and use and make a record of it."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b52422beac69900214e084249891ce14d6595b33650715e70a97f79177accdb8" ;
