concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-67-ss-1b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "67(1B) Dealing for permitted purposes"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-67-ss-1b ;
    values:originalText "(1B) However, an officer or staff member of an agency may communicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of information mentioned in paragraph (1A)(a), (b) or (c) for a purpose or purposes set out in subsection (1C), and for no other purpose, if the information has not been communicated to an officer of the agency under section 68." ;
    skos:definition "(1B) However, an officer or staff member of an agency may communicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of information mentioned in paragraph (1A)(a), (b) or (c) for a purpose or purposes set out in subsection (1C), and for no other purpose, if the information has not been communicated to an officer of the agency under section 68."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "eccf83b64742b06e1aaacbd2a8b56eb5aeab33476f6f33b448f7bafdfa8a7060" ;
