doc:sec-67-ss-1b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "67(1B) Dealing for permitted purposes" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1B) However, an officer or staff member of an agency may communicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of information mentioned in paragraph (1A)(a), (b) or (c) for a purpose or purposes set out in subsection (1C), and for no other purpose, if the information has not been communicated to an officer of the agency under section 68." ;
    cof:pageNumber "232"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-67-ss-1c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "67(1C) Dealing for permitted purposes"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-67-ss-1c ;
    values:originalText "(1C) The purposes are purposes connected with:  (a) if the warrant under which the information was obtained relates to an investigation—the investigation; or  (b) if the information was obtained under a Part 5.3 warrant issued on the basis that a Part 5.3 supervisory order was in force in relation to a person—any of the following:  (i) achieving a Part 5.3 object;  (ii) determining whether the Part 5.3 supervisory order has been, or is being, complied with; or  (c) if the information was obtained under any Part 5.3 warrant— the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of a power, by a person, court or other body under, or in relation to a matter arising under:  (i) Division 104 (control orders) or Division 105A (post-sentence orders) of the Criminal Code; or  (ii) a post-sentence detention order or a post-sentence supervision order; or  (iii) a preventative detention order law; or  (d) if the information was obtained under a Part 9.10 warrant issued on the basis that a community safety supervision order was in force in relation to a person—any of the following:  (i) achieving a Part 9.10 object;  (ii) determining whether the community safety supervision order has been, or is being, complied with; or  (e) if the information was obtained under any Part 9.10 warrant—the performance of a function or duty, or the  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications" ;
    skos:definition "(1C) The purposes are purposes connected with:  (a) if the warrant under which the information was obtained relates to an investigation—the investigation; or  (b) if the information was obtained under a Part 5.3 warrant issued on the basis that a Part 5.3 supervisory order was in force in relation to a person—any of the following:  (i) achieving a Part 5.3 object;  (ii) determining whether the Part 5.3 supervisory order has been, or is being, complied with; or  (c) if the information was obtained under any Part 5.3 warrant— the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of a power, by a person, court or other body under, or in relation to a matter arising under:  (i) Division 104 (control orders) or Division 105A (post-sentence orders) of the Criminal Code; or  (ii) a post-sentence detention order or a post-sentence supervision order; or  (iii) a preventative detention order law; or  (d) if the information was obtained under a Part 9.10 warrant issued on the basis that a community safety supervision order was in force in relation to a person—any of the following:  (i) achieving a Part 9.10 object;  (ii) determining whether the community safety supervision order has been, or is being, complied with; or  (e) if the information was obtained under any Part 9.10 warrant—the performance of a function or duty, or the  Chapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "940dc55fcd36af6d1cd335cdf28ed820202b8d5120508ba3b933013ff33f44d9" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-67 ;
    cof:pageNumber "232"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The purposes are purposes connected with the investigation, achieving a Part 5.3 object, determining compliance, or performing a function/duty related to specific laws." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
