doc:sec-75-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "75(1) Giving information in evidence where defect in connection with" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Where a communication has been intercepted in contravention of subsection 7(1) but purportedly under a warrant (other than a general computer access warrant, a data disruption warrant, a network activity warrant or a warrant under section 11A, 11B or 11C), a person may give information obtained by the interception in evidence in an exempt proceeding, being a proceeding in a court or before a tribunal, body, authority or person, if the court, tribunal, body, authority or person, as the case may be, is satisfied that:  (a) but for an irregularity, the interception would not have constituted a contravention of subsection 7(1); and  (b) in all the circumstances, the irregularity should be disregarded." ;
    cof:pageNumber "245"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-75-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "75(2) Giving information in evidence where defect in connection with"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-75-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A reference in subsection (1) to an irregularity is a reference to a defect or irregularity (other than a substantial defect or irregularity):  (a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting to be a warrant; or  (b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the purported execution of a document purporting to be a warrant." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A reference in subsection (1) to an irregularity is a reference to a defect or irregularity (other than a substantial defect or irregularity):  (a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting to be a warrant; or  (b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the purported execution of a document purporting to be a warrant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8055acfb2c3808c8bf725d793665075a023bac7fe590542935004038ebb1e513" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-75 ;
