doc:sec-81d-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "81D(2) Regular submission of Special Register to Minister" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Once at least within each succeeding period of 3 months, the Secretary of the Department must deliver to the Minister, for inspection by the Minister, any part of the Special Register that represents information recorded since the Special Register, or any part of the Special Register, was last delivered to the Minister. Special Register and General Register to be delivered at the same time" ;
    cof:pageNumber "259"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-81d-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "81D(3) Regular submission of Special Register to Minister"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-81d-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) As far as is practicable, the Secretary of the Department is to ensure that delivery of the Special Register, or a part of the Special Register, as the case requires, takes place at the same time as the delivery of a part of the General Register under subsection 81B(2)." ;
    skos:definition "(3) As far as is practicable, the Secretary of the Department is to ensure that delivery of the Special Register, or a part of the Special Register, as the case requires, takes place at the same time as the delivery of a part of the General Register under subsection 81B(2)."@en ;
