    values:originalText "(3) The report must contain the following information:  (a) if an interception occurred:  (i) the date and time at which the interception began; and  (ii) the duration of the interception;  (b) if there was no interception but action had been taken to cause a communication to be intercepted—details of the action taken;  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Reports about interceptions under Parts 2-3 and 2-5  Part 2-8 Reports to the Minister  Division 1  Section 94B  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) the circumstances that led the officer concerned to believe that the conditions of subsection 7(4) or (5) were satisfied;  (d) in the case set out in paragraph (1)(a)—the reasons it was not practicable to apply for a warrant under Part 2-5 in relation to the action;  (e) in the case set out in paragraph (1)(b)—the reasons the judge or nominated ART member refused the application if the reasons are known;  (f) information about the use made by the agency of information obtained by the interception;  (g) information about the communication of such information to persons other than officers of the agency;  (h) the number of arrests that have been, or are likely to be, made on the basis of such information;  (i) an assessment of the usefulness of information obtained by the interception." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The report must contain the following information:  (a) if an interception occurred:  (i) the date and time at which the interception began; and  (ii) the duration of the interception;  (b) if there was no interception but action had been taken to cause a communication to be intercepted—details of the action taken;  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Reports about interceptions under Parts 2-3 and 2-5  Part 2-8 Reports to the Minister  Division 1  Section 94B  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) the circumstances that led the officer concerned to believe that the conditions of subsection 7(4) or (5) were satisfied;  (d) in the case set out in paragraph (1)(a)—the reasons it was not practicable to apply for a warrant under Part 2-5 in relation to the action;  (e) in the case set out in paragraph (1)(b)—the reasons the judge or nominated ART member refused the application if the reasons are known;  (f) information about the use made by the agency of information obtained by the interception;  (g) information about the communication of such information to persons other than officers of the agency;  (h) the number of arrests that have been, or are likely to be, made on the basis of such information;  (i) an assessment of the usefulness of information obtained by the interception."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "552cf7bf4685ae63081e831a125231cde88b11d22484b58f90700bfb5b1bfbbc" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-94a ;
    cof:pageNumber "272"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Report requirements for emergency interception action" ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
