doc:sec-95-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "95(2) Minister may seek further information from Commonwealth" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) To the extent that it is practicable to do so, the chief officer of a Commonwealth agency, or eligible Commonwealth authority, shall comply with a request made to the chief officer under subsection (1)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "274"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-96 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "96 Annual reports by State authorities"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-96 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the chief officer of an eligible authority of a State shall, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report that:  (a) if information that section 102 or 102A requires to be set out in the Minister’s report under Division 2 relating to the year  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Reports about interceptions under Parts 2-3 and 2-5  Part 2-8 Reports to the Minister  Division 1  Section 97  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  ending on that 30 June can be derived from the authority’s records—sets out that information; or  (b) in any other case—states that no such information can be so derived.  (1A) A report under subsection (1) must include a statement of the total expenditure (including expenditure of a capital nature) incurred by the eligible authority concerned in connection with the execution of warrants during the year to which the report relates.  (2) Where a Minister of a State has given to the Minister a written report that sets out the information that, but for this subsection, subsections (1) and (1A) would require to be set out in a report by the chief officer of an eligible authority of that State, the chief officer need not give to the Minister the last-mentioned report." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the chief officer of an eligible authority of a State shall, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report that:  (a) if information that section 102 or 102A requires to be set out in the Minister’s report under Division 2 relating to the year  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Reports about interceptions under Parts 2-3 and 2-5  Part 2-8 Reports to the Minister  Division 1  Section 97  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  ending on that 30 June can be derived from the authority’s records—sets out that information; or  (b) in any other case—states that no such information can be so derived.  (1A) A report under subsection (1) must include a statement of the total expenditure (including expenditure of a capital nature) incurred by the eligible authority concerned in connection with the execution of warrants during the year to which the report relates.  (2) Where a Minister of a State has given to the Minister a written report that sets out the information that, but for this subsection, subsections (1) and (1A) would require to be set out in a report by the chief officer of an eligible authority of that State, the chief officer need not give to the Minister the last-mentioned report."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2e942d6012dbeabbcac5ee0ca3c7427ca0fe6474df2dfb8e804ba6e417238909" ;
    cof:pageNumber "274"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-96-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-96-ss-1a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-96-ss-2 ;
