concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-106 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "106 Obstruction"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-106 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person shall not obstruct or hinder a person acting under a warrant. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Offences  Part 2-9  Section 107  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person obstructing or hindering has a reasonable excuse. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person shall not obstruct or hinder a person acting under a warrant. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.  Interception of telecommunications  Chapter 2 Offences  Part 2-9  Section 107  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person obstructing or hindering has a reasonable excuse. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "52523ad1a9cd09bfe1a9ccb79d7f72094f6304d11303449872f1f14fdfc8d13f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "290"^^xsd:integer ;
