concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "107F Extended meaning of conviction—orders under section 19B of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-107f ;
    values:originalText "the Crimes Act 1914  A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence. Note: Section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 empowers a court that has found a person to have committed an offence to take action without proceeding to record a conviction.  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Preserving stored communications  Part 3-1A Outline of this Part  Division 1  Section 107G  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Chapter 3—Preserving and accessing stored communications" ;
    skos:definition "the Crimes Act 1914  A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence. Note: Section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 empowers a court that has found a person to have committed an offence to take action without proceeding to record a conviction.  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Preserving stored communications  Part 3-1A Outline of this Part  Division 1  Section 107G  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Chapter 3—Preserving and accessing stored communications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "57aabcc9d76e0b8ab9b1f309248bd1917b49d1d26a0d4376a779a93d0d489107" ;
    cof:pageNumber "296"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.296" ;
