concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-113 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "113 Affidavits to accompany written applications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-113 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The application must, if it is in writing, be accompanied by an affidavit complying with this section.  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Access by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3 Applications for warrants  Division 1  Section 114  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) The affidavit must set out the facts and other grounds on which the application is based.  (3) Despite subsection (1), a written application may be accompanied by 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, but for this subsection, this section would have required an affidavit accompanying the application to set out." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The application must, if it is in writing, be accompanied by an affidavit complying with this section.  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Access by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3 Applications for warrants  Division 1  Section 114  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) The affidavit must set out the facts and other grounds on which the application is based.  (3) Despite subsection (1), a written application may be accompanied by 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, but for this subsection, this section would have required an affidavit accompanying the application to set out."@en ;
