concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-115 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "115 Giving further information to Judge"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-115 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An issuing authority may require further information to be given in connection with an application to the issuing authority for a warrant.  (2) The further information:  (a) must be given on oath if the application was made in writing; and  (b) must be given orally or otherwise, as the issuing authority directs.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An issuing authority may require further information to be given in connection with an application to the issuing authority for a warrant.  (2) The further information:  (a) must be given on oath if the application was made in writing; and  (b) must be given orally or otherwise, as the issuing authority directs.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8f183acff0df39f6112e88c3698d375d515f6f398df627f6692d8af49c79955c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "321"^^xsd:integer ;
