doc:sec-120-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "120(2) Stored communications warrants issued on telephone" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person who makes a telephone application on a criminal law-enforcement agency’s behalf must, within one day after the day on which a warrant is issued on the application:  (a) cause each person who gave information to the issuing authority in connection with the application to swear an affidavit setting out the information so given by the person; and  (b) give to the issuing authority:  (i) the affidavit or affidavits; and  (ii) unless the applicant is the chief officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency—a copy of an authorisation by the chief officer under subsection 111(3) that was in force in relation to the applicant when the application was made." ;
    cof:pageNumber "326"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "120(3) Stored communications warrants issued on telephone"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-120-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) An issuing authority may, by writing signed by him or her, revoke a warrant that he or she issued on a telephone application if satisfied that subsection (2) has not been complied with in relation to the warrant. If he or she does so, he or she must:  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Access by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3 How warrants etc. are dealt with  Division 3  Section 121  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) forthwith inform the person who made the application on the criminal law-enforcement agency’s behalf, or the chief officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency, of the revocation; and  (b) give the instrument of revocation to that person, or to the chief officer, as soon as practicable." ;
    skos:definition "(3) An issuing authority may, by writing signed by him or her, revoke a warrant that he or she issued on a telephone application if satisfied that subsection (2) has not been complied with in relation to the warrant. If he or she does so, he or she must:  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Access by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3 How warrants etc. are dealt with  Division 3  Section 121  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) forthwith inform the person who made the application on the criminal law-enforcement agency’s behalf, or the chief officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency, of the revocation; and  (b) give the instrument of revocation to that person, or to the chief officer, as soon as practicable."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "674f9036edda9d93f71b0f7bf8e3e981d7d480c91e56bf480043aeca4b94865a" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120 ;
    cof:pageNumber "326"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Revocation of warrant issued on telephone application" ;
    dc:description "inform the person who made the application and give the instrument of revocation" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
