concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-122 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "122 Revocation of stored communications warrants by chief officers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-122 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency to which a stored communications warrant has been issued must, on being satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have ceased to exist:  (a) cause the chief officer of any other criminal law-enforcement agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and  (b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency to which a stored communications warrant has been issued must, on being satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have ceased to exist:  (a) cause the chief officer of any other criminal law-enforcement agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and  (b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "045d7461e9692f36bc761401f7b1af89205b0a29533f974bd33eda33d7c48123" ;
    cof:pageNumber "327"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Chief officer must inform and revoke stored communications warrant." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
