doc:sec-122 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "122 Revocation of stored communications warrants by chief officers" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency to which a stored communications warrant has been issued must, on being satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have ceased to exist:  (a) cause the chief officer of any other criminal law-enforcement agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and  (b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications" ;
    cof:pageNumber "327"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-123 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "123 What happens when stored communications warrants are"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-123 ;
    values:originalText "revoked  (1) Upon revoking a stored communications warrant, the chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency must cause the chief officer of any other criminal law-enforcement agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the revocation.  (2) If an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed, under section 121, of the issue of a stored communications warrant and that warrant is subsequently revoked, the chief officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency to which the warrant was issued must:  (a) cause that authorised representative to be informed forthwith of the revocation; and  (b) cause a copy of the instrument of revocation, certified in writing by a certifying officer to be a true copy of the instrument, to be given as soon as practicable to that authorised representative." ;
    skos:definition "revoked  (1) Upon revoking a stored communications warrant, the chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency must cause the chief officer of any other criminal law-enforcement agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the revocation.  (2) If an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed, under section 121, of the issue of a stored communications warrant and that warrant is subsequently revoked, the chief officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency to which the warrant was issued must:  (a) cause that authorised representative to be informed forthwith of the revocation; and  (b) cause a copy of the instrument of revocation, certified in writing by a certifying officer to be a true copy of the instrument, to be given as soon as practicable to that authorised representative."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4bb47f186df233e48b09d241ee4defb821add0c35ac8311469fe1522c6813dd5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "328"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-123-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-123-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.328" .
doc:sec-123 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "123 What happens when stored communications warrants are" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "revoked  (1) Upon revoking a stored communications warrant, the chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency must cause the chief officer of any other criminal law-enforcement agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the revocation.  (2) If an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed, under section 121, of the issue of a stored communications warrant and that warrant is subsequently revoked, the chief officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency to which the warrant was issued must:  (a) cause that authorised representative to be informed forthwith of the revocation; and  (b) cause a copy of the instrument of revocation, certified in writing by a certifying officer to be a true copy of the instrument, to be given as soon as practicable to that authorised representative." ;
    cof:pageNumber "328"^^xsd:integer .

