concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-127-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "127(3) Exercise of authority conferred by warrant"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-127-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may appoint in writing an officer of the agency to be an approving officer for the purposes of subsection (2).  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Access by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3 Provisions relating to execution of warrants  Division 4  Section 128  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may appoint in writing an officer of the agency to be an approving officer for the purposes of subsection (2).  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Access by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3 Provisions relating to execution of warrants  Division 4  Section 128  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1a435ea0361fe6979c087b725c426b57d2491d9119d48470bdd2c3822fc0c9b6" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-127 ;
    cof:pageNumber "330"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Chief officer may appoint an approving officer." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
