concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-130 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "130 Evidentiary certificates relating to actions by criminal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-130 ;
    values:originalText "law-enforcement agencies  (1) A certifying officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such facts as he or she considers relevant with respect to:  (a) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in connection with the execution of a stored communications warrant; or  (b) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in connection with:  (i) the communication by a person to another person of information obtained by the execution of such a warrant; or  (ii) the making use of such information; or  (iii) the making of a record of such information; or  (iv) the custody of a record of such information; or  (v) the giving in evidence of such information.  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Access by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3 Provisions relating to execution of warrants  Division 4  Section 131  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under this section by a certifying officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency and to be signed by him or her:  (a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding without further proof; and  (b) in an exempt proceeding, is prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the document." ;
    skos:definition "law-enforcement agencies  (1) A certifying officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such facts as he or she considers relevant with respect to:  (a) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in connection with the execution of a stored communications warrant; or  (b) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in connection with:  (i) the communication by a person to another person of information obtained by the execution of such a warrant; or  (ii) the making use of such information; or  (iii) the making of a record of such information; or  (iv) the custody of a record of such information; or  (v) the giving in evidence of such information.  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Access by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3 Provisions relating to execution of warrants  Division 4  Section 131  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under this section by a certifying officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency and to be signed by him or her:  (a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding without further proof; and  (b) in an exempt proceeding, is prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the document."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f85488adc04fb61660b743b0e6cf473ccee1f33c9d577829e7b2cde21bbbd686" ;
    cof:pageNumber "332"^^xsd:integer ;
