doc:sec-145 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "145 Evidence that has been given in exempt proceeding" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If information is given in evidence in an exempt proceeding under section 143 or 144, that information, or any part of that information, may later be given in evidence in any proceeding. Note: This section was inserted as a response to the decision of the Court of Appeal of New South Wales in Wood v Beves (1997) 92 A Crim R 209.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications" ;
    cof:pageNumber "347"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-146 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "146 Giving information in evidence in civil proceedings for remedial"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-146 ;
    values:originalText "relief  (1) A person may give information obtained by accessing a stored communication in contravention of subsection 108(1) in evidence in a proceeding by way of an application under section 165 for remedial relief in respect of:  (a) the access; or  (b) the communication (in contravention of section 133) of information obtained by the access.  (2) A person may give preservation notice information or stored communications warrant information in evidence in a proceeding by way of an application under section 165.  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Dealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4 Admissibility of evidence  Division 3  Section 147  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "relief  (1) A person may give information obtained by accessing a stored communication in contravention of subsection 108(1) in evidence in a proceeding by way of an application under section 165 for remedial relief in respect of:  (a) the access; or  (b) the communication (in contravention of section 133) of information obtained by the access.  (2) A person may give preservation notice information or stored communications warrant information in evidence in a proceeding by way of an application under section 165.  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Dealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4 Admissibility of evidence  Division 3  Section 147  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ea6a344e27604dcb67a09c548bcf44b13628c54debf48bcf37139db8f9f9dd86" ;
    cof:pageNumber "348"^^xsd:integer ;
