    cof:pageNumber "350"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-150 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "150 Destruction of records"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-150 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) information, or a record, that was obtained by accessing a stored communication (whether or not in contravention of subsection 108(1)) is in a criminal law-enforcement agency’s possession; and  (b) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the information or record is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to in subsection 139(2) or (4A), 139A(2) or 139B(2); the chief officer must cause the information or record to be destroyed forthwith.  (2) The chief officer must, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report that sets out the extent to which information and records were destroyed in accordance with this section.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) information, or a record, that was obtained by accessing a stored communication (whether or not in contravention of subsection 108(1)) is in a criminal law-enforcement agency’s possession; and  (b) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the information or record is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to in subsection 139(2) or (4A), 139A(2) or 139B(2); the chief officer must cause the information or record to be destroyed forthwith.  (2) The chief officer must, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report that sets out the extent to which information and records were destroyed in accordance with this section.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "085d5e7155f0aa7a250679b548526a2798ee1f0c8bd23edd8df38a27c9ad0c4d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "351"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-150-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-150-ss-2 ;
