doc:sec-150-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "150(1) Destruction of records" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) information, or a record, that was obtained by accessing a stored communication (whether or not in contravention of subsection 108(1)) is in a criminal law-enforcement agency’s possession; and  (b) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the information or record is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to in subsection 139(2) or (4A), 139A(2) or 139B(2); the chief officer must cause the information or record to be destroyed forthwith." ;
    cof:pageNumber "351"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-150-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "150(2) Destruction of records"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-150-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The chief officer must, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report that sets out the extent to which information and records were destroyed in accordance with this section.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The chief officer must, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report that sets out the extent to which information and records were destroyed in accordance with this section.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f8e053031ab31fffea9ee3db37778bd1f980e2a0551ef191dd571b879071ec0d" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-150 ;
    cof:pageNumber "351"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Chief officer must provide a written report on record destruction within 3 months after June 30th." ;
    dc:description "true" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
