doc:sec-158a-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "158A(2) Functions of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) In particular, the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security has the function of:  (a) inquiring into any matter that relates to compliance by the Organisation with this Act (see subparagraph 8(1)(a)(i) of that Act); and  (b) conducting such inspections of the Organisation as the Inspector-General considers appropriate for the purpose of giving effect to the objects of that Act (see section 9A of that Act).  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Reports about access to stored communications  Part 3-6 Reports to the Minister  Division 1  Section 159  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "354"^^xsd:integer .

