concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-160 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "160 Minister may seek further information from Commonwealth"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-160 ;
    values:originalText "agency  (1) The Minister may, by writing, request the chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency to give to the Minister in writing specified information that:  (a) the Minister needs in connection with preparing a report under Division 2; and  (b) is not contained in a report by the chief officer under section 159.  (2) To the extent that it is practicable to do so, the chief officer must comply with the request.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications" ;
    skos:definition "agency  (1) The Minister may, by writing, request the chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency to give to the Minister in writing specified information that:  (a) the Minister needs in connection with preparing a report under Division 2; and  (b) is not contained in a report by the chief officer under section 159.  (2) To the extent that it is practicable to do so, the chief officer must comply with the request.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c4b2af4722ee54e317672875b2d8cf49aa884bf5820ec6091114fea5ec6560e4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "355"^^xsd:integer ;
