concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "165(2) Civil remedies—unlawful access or communication"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-165-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of this section, a person is an aggrieved person if, and only if:  (a) the person was a party to the communication; or  (b) the communication was made on the person’s behalf. Access—civil court remedy" ;
    skos:definition "(2) For the purposes of this section, a person is an aggrieved person if, and only if:  (a) the person was a party to the communication; or  (b) the communication was made on the person’s behalf. Access—civil court remedy"@en ;
