concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "165(4) Civil remedies—unlawful access or communication"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-165-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If:  (a) information was obtained by accessing the communication; and  (b) a person (the defendant) communicated the information to another person in contravention of section 133;  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Civil remedies  Part 3-7  Section 165  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  the Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the communication of the information by making such orders against the defendant as the court considers appropriate. Access—criminal court remedy" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If:  (a) information was obtained by accessing the communication; and  (b) a person (the defendant) communicated the information to another person in contravention of section 133;  Preserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3 Civil remedies  Part 3-7  Section 165  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  the Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the communication of the information by making such orders against the defendant as the court considers appropriate. Access—criminal court remedy"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5f1fd29353c8d5915e50644e0eacde7e3a1dfc1ec16501eb9b37dfbaaf8e432f" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165 ;
