concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "165(6) Civil remedies—unlawful access or communication"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-165-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) If:  (a) information was obtained by accessing the communication; and  (b) the information was communicated to a person in contravention of section 133; and  (c) a court convicts a person (in this subsection called the defendant) of an offence against section 133 constituted by the communication of the information; the court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the communication of the information by making such orders against the defendant as the court considers appropriate.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications" ;
    skos:definition "(6) If:  (a) information was obtained by accessing the communication; and  (b) the information was communicated to a person in contravention of section 133; and  (c) a court convicts a person (in this subsection called the defendant) of an offence against section 133 constituted by the communication of the information; the court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the communication of the information by making such orders against the defendant as the court considers appropriate.  Chapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ce153bda5a29ff2d9b7c0fec83351260ee983d7a91c6554e6207addc86d50bd3" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165 ;
