concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-170 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "170 Extended meaning of conviction—orders under section 19B of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-170 ;
    values:originalText "the Crimes Act 1914  A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence. Note: Section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 empowers a court that has found a person to have committed an offence to take action without proceeding to record a conviction.  Access to telecommunications data  Chapter 4 Permitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1 Outline of Part  Division 1  Section 171  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Chapter 4—Access to telecommunications data" ;
    skos:definition "the Crimes Act 1914  A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence. Note: Section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 empowers a court that has found a person to have committed an offence to take action without proceeding to record a conviction.  Access to telecommunications data  Chapter 4 Permitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1 Outline of Part  Division 1  Section 171  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Chapter 4—Access to telecommunications data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e9f27093907f232d4571166a19d5f255693e4ada442dbe544af1860262f0e7f4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "364"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
