concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-170 cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-170-logic-ltl-4 .
concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-170-logic-ltl-4 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:LTL ;
    cml:operator "includes" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Includes the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence." ;
    cml:premiseText "A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to..." ;
    cml:conclusionText "...the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::temporal_ltl" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-170 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "170 Extended meaning of conviction—orders under section 19B of" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "the Crimes Act 1914  A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence. Note: Section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 empowers a court that has found a person to have committed an offence to take action without proceeding to record a conviction.  Access to telecommunications data  Chapter 4 Permitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1 Outline of Part  Division 1  Section 171  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Chapter 4—Access to telecommunications data" ;
    cof:pageNumber "364"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-171 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "171 Outline of Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-171 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Divisions 3, 4 and 4A set out some circumstances when sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not prohibit a disclosure of information or a document. Note 1: Division 3 covers the Organisation. Division 4 covers disclosures for the purposes of Australian enforcement agencies. Division 4A covers disclosures for the purposes of foreign law enforcement. Note 2: Those Divisions do not permit the disclosure of the contents or substance of a communication: see Division 2.  (2) Division 5 sets out some circumstances when sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not prohibit a use of information or a document.  (3) Division 6 creates offences for certain disclosures and uses of information and documents.  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Divisions 3, 4 and 4A set out some circumstances when sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not prohibit a disclosure of information or a document. Note 1: Division 3 covers the Organisation. Division 4 covers disclosures for the purposes of Australian enforcement agencies. Division 4A covers disclosures for the purposes of foreign law enforcement. Note 2: Those Divisions do not permit the disclosure of the contents or substance of a communication: see Division 2.  (2) Division 5 sets out some circumstances when sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not prohibit a use of information or a document.  (3) Division 6 creates offences for certain disclosures and uses of information and documents.  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4201999979a760c0a985986d2c8b24c534b177027c55c607c08311972f3c1321" ;
