concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "177 Voluntary disclosure"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-177 ;
    values:originalText "Enforcement of the criminal law  (1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not prevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or a document to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is reasonably necessary for the enforcement of the criminal law.  Access to telecommunications data  Chapter 4 Permitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1 Enforcement agencies  Division 4  Section 178  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty or protection of the public revenue  (2) Sections 276 and 277 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not prevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or a document to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is reasonably necessary for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty or for the protection of the public revenue. Limitation  (3) This section does not apply if a relevant staff member of an enforcement agency requests the holder to disclose the information or document. Note: Sections 178 to 180 deal with the disclosure of information or a document in response to authorisations by an authorised officer of an enforcement agency." ;
    skos:definition "Enforcement of the criminal law  (1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not prevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or a document to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is reasonably necessary for the enforcement of the criminal law.  Access to telecommunications data  Chapter 4 Permitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1 Enforcement agencies  Division 4  Section 178  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty or protection of the public revenue  (2) Sections 276 and 277 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not prevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or a document to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is reasonably necessary for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty or for the protection of the public revenue. Limitation  (3) This section does not apply if a relevant staff member of an enforcement agency requests the holder to disclose the information or document. Note: Sections 178 to 180 deal with the disclosure of information or a document in response to authorisations by an authorised officer of an enforcement agency."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b7b7836deb029f31e8c3b1b967675bde4cbccc8d47a80432c241083b9febef93" ;
    cof:pageNumber "372"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177-ss-2 ;
