doc:sec-180d-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "180D(1) Authorisations to disclose information or documents—" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If specified information or specified documents are disclosed because of an authorisation given under this Division, an authorised officer of the Australian Federal Police may authorise the following:  (a) the disclosure of the information or documents to the Organisation or an enforcement agency;  (b) the use of the information or documents by the Australian Federal Police." ;
    cof:pageNumber "381"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180d-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "180D(2) Authorisations to disclose information or documents—"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-180d-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or she is satisfied that:  (a) in the case of a disclosure to the Organisation—the disclosure is reasonably necessary for the performance by the Organisation of its functions; and  (b) in the case of a disclosure to an enforcement agency—the disclosure is reasonably necessary:  (i) for the enforcement of the criminal law; or  (ia) for the purposes of Division 105A of the Criminal Code (post-sentence orders); or  (ib) for the purposes of Division 395 of the Criminal Code (community safety orders); or  (ii) for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty; or  (iii) for the protection of the public revenue; and  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or she is satisfied that:  (a) in the case of a disclosure to the Organisation—the disclosure is reasonably necessary for the performance by the Organisation of its functions; and  (b) in the case of a disclosure to an enforcement agency—the disclosure is reasonably necessary:  (i) for the enforcement of the criminal law; or  (ia) for the purposes of Division 105A of the Criminal Code (post-sentence orders); or  (ib) for the purposes of Division 395 of the Criminal Code (community safety orders); or  (ii) for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty; or  (iii) for the protection of the public revenue; and  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fa50591477d98a73d99a66a20fb2fac0fdc3e51bcbc394bd75496cc37597cbb5" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180d ;
    cof:pageNumber "381"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorised officer must make disclosure only if necessary for Organisation's functions or enforcement of laws." ;
