    values:originalText "(1) An authorised officer of an enforcement agency must not make an authorisation under section 178, 178A, 179 or 180 that would authorise the disclosure of information or documents relating to a particular person if:  (a) the authorised officer knows or reasonably believes that particular person to be:  (i) a person who is working in a professional capacity as a journalist; or  Access to telecommunications data  Chapter 4 Permitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1 Journalist information warrants  Division 4C  Section 180J  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (ii) an employer of such a person; and  (b) a purpose of making the authorisation would be to identify another person whom the authorised officer knows or reasonably believes to be a source; unless a journalist information warrant is in force, in relation to that particular person, under which authorised officers of the agency may make authorisations under that section." ;
    cof:pageNumber "384"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180h-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "180H(2) Enforcement agencies"@en ;
