concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "180K Further information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-180k ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General may require the Director-General of Security to give to the Attorney-General, within the period specified in the requirement, further information in connection with a request under this Subdivision.  (2) If the Director-General breaches the requirement, the Attorney-General may:  (a) refuse to consider the request; or  (b) refuse to take any action, or any further action, in relation to the request." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Attorney-General may require the Director-General of Security to give to the Attorney-General, within the period specified in the requirement, further information in connection with a request under this Subdivision.  (2) If the Director-General breaches the requirement, the Attorney-General may:  (a) refuse to consider the request; or  (b) refuse to take any action, or any further action, in relation to the request."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5d648ca7cd8f02c4f41c4fba333382c1ea2c48480284bbc7f734a84e8b07b22d" ;
