concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180m a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "180M Issuing a journalist information warrant in an emergency"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-180m ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Director-General of Security may issue a journalist information warrant in relation to a particular person if:  (a) a request under section 180J has been made for the issue of a journalist information warrant in relation to the particular person; and  (b) the Attorney-General has not, to the knowledge of the Director-General, made a decision under section 180L in relation to the request; and  (c) within the preceding period of 3 months:  (i) the Attorney-General has not refused to issue a journalist information warrant in relation to the particular person; and  (ii) the Director-General has not issued such a journalist information warrant; and  (d) the Director-General is satisfied that, security will be, or is likely to be, seriously prejudiced if the access to which the request relates does not begin before a journalist information warrant can be issued and made available by the Attorney-General; and  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Director-General of Security may issue a journalist information warrant in relation to a particular person if:  (a) a request under section 180J has been made for the issue of a journalist information warrant in relation to the particular person; and  (b) the Attorney-General has not, to the knowledge of the Director-General, made a decision under section 180L in relation to the request; and  (c) within the preceding period of 3 months:  (i) the Attorney-General has not refused to issue a journalist information warrant in relation to the particular person; and  (ii) the Director-General has not issued such a journalist information warrant; and  (d) the Director-General is satisfied that, security will be, or is likely to be, seriously prejudiced if the access to which the request relates does not begin before a journalist information warrant can be issued and made available by the Attorney-General; and  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9106cb98ccf188f2817f373c91b1c3aa3c8010879d524dc50e4afab1af056e22" ;
    cof:pageNumber "387"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Director-General must issue a journalist information warrant in an emergency." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
