concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-182 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "182 Secondary disclosure/use offence: disclosures under Division 4"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-182 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information or a document is disclosed to the person as permitted by Division 4 or 4A; and  (b) the person discloses or uses the information or document. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years. Exempt disclosures  (2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a disclosure of non-missing person information if:  (a) the disclosure is reasonably necessary:  (i) for a person to comply with his or her obligations under section 185D or 185E; or  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information or a document is disclosed to the person as permitted by Division 4 or 4A; and  (b) the person discloses or uses the information or document. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years. Exempt disclosures  (2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a disclosure of non-missing person information if:  (a) the disclosure is reasonably necessary:  (i) for a person to comply with his or her obligations under section 185D or 185E; or  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "41903fc72b7aca8517d43b1327eb5bbb3b6088fbbbb850af048e729eacb8ad52" ;
    cof:pageNumber "401"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-182-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-182-ss-2 ;
