concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "185 Retention of authorisations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-185 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The head (however described) of an enforcement agency must retain an authorisation made under Division 4 of Part 4-1 by an authorised officer of the enforcement agency for the period of 3 years beginning on the day the authorisation is made.  (2) The Commissioner of Police must retain an authorisation made under Division 4A of Part 4-1 by an authorised officer of the  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The head (however described) of an enforcement agency must retain an authorisation made under Division 4 of Part 4-1 by an authorised officer of the enforcement agency for the period of 3 years beginning on the day the authorisation is made.  (2) The Commissioner of Police must retain an authorisation made under Division 4A of Part 4-1 by an authorised officer of the  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b8dbafefcdf398addbc499166d44e337b6cc6ddee06b6f7b1fd237bffdf39e91" ;
    cof:pageNumber "407"^^xsd:integer ;
