doc:sec-185b-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "185B(2) Evidentiary certificates relating to acts by the Organisation" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under subsection (1) by the Director-General of Security or the Deputy Director-General of Security and to be signed by him or her:  (a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding without further proof; and  (b) is, in an exempt proceeding, prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the document." ;
    cof:pageNumber "409"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "185C Evidentiary certificates relating to acts by enforcement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-185c ;
    values:originalText "agencies  (1) A certifying officer of an enforcement agency may issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such facts as he or she considers relevant with respect to:  (a) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in connection with the disclosure of information or a document  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data" ;
    skos:definition "agencies  (1) A certifying officer of an enforcement agency may issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such facts as he or she considers relevant with respect to:  (a) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in connection with the disclosure of information or a document  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "42618902074b432971ac565e37ebee07fb3ff4e3d23dcdef15664585d27d47b8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "409"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Certifying officer must issue written certificate setting out relevant facts." ;
