    values:originalText "(5) If a journalist information warrant is issued to an enforcement agency:  (aa) if the agency was the ACC:  (i) the chief officer of the ACC must, as soon as practicable, give copies of the warrant to the Minister and the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security; and  (ii) the Minister must, as soon as practicable after receiving a copy, cause the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security to be notified of the issuing of the warrant; and  Chapter 4  Access to telecommunications data" ;
