doc:sec-186b-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "186B(1) Inspection of records" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Ombudsman must inspect records of an enforcement agency, except the ACC or any agency, or part of an agency performing any functions, prescribed by regulations made under the Ombudsman Act 1976 for the purposes of subsection (1B) of this section, to determine:  (a) the extent of compliance with Chapter 4 by the agency and its officers; and  (b) if the agency is a criminal law-enforcement agency, except the ACC or any agency, or part of an agency performing any functions, prescribed by regulations made under the Ombudsman Act 1976 for the purposes of subsection (1B) of this section—the extent of compliance with Chapter 3 by the agency and its officers." ;
    cof:pageNumber "421"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186b-ss-1a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "186B(1A) Inspection of records"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-186b-ss-1a ;
    values:originalText "(1A) If:  (a) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a power, conferred by Part 15 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 is in connection with:  (i) a stored communications warrant; or  (ii) an authorisation under Division 3, 4 or 4A of Part 4-1; and  (b) an enforcement agency, except the ACC or any agency, or part of an agency performing any functions, prescribed by regulations made under the Ombudsman Act 1976 for the purposes of subsection (1B) of this section, has records that relate to the performance of that function or the exercise of that power; the Ombudsman may inspect those records in order to determine the extent of compliance with Part 15 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 by the agency and its officers.  Chapter 4A  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Section 186B  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1A) If:  (a) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a power, conferred by Part 15 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 is in connection with:  (i) a stored communications warrant; or  (ii) an authorisation under Division 3, 4 or 4A of Part 4-1; and  (b) an enforcement agency, except the ACC or any agency, or part of an agency performing any functions, prescribed by regulations made under the Ombudsman Act 1976 for the purposes of subsection (1B) of this section, has records that relate to the performance of that function or the exercise of that power; the Ombudsman may inspect those records in order to determine the extent of compliance with Part 15 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 by the agency and its officers.  Chapter 4A  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Section 186B  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2ed7fab2ed404fe15a8c42cfe6204b0d5d25485d495882e4dd30661ecdf2fa0b" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186b ;
    cof:pageNumber "421"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Ombudsman may inspect records to determine compliance with Part 15 of the Telecommunications Act 1997." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.421" ;
