doc:sec-186b-ss-1b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "186B(1B) Inspection of records" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1B) Regulations made under the Ombudsman Act 1976 may prescribe certain agencies, or functions of certain agencies, for the purposes of this subsection." ;
    cof:pageNumber "421"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186b-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "186B(2) Inspection of records"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-186b-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this section, the Ombudsman:  (a) after notifying the chief officer of the agency, may enter at any reasonable time premises occupied by the agency; and  (b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times to all records of the agency that are relevant to the inspection; and  (c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to take extracts from, records of the agency; and  (d) may require a member of staff of the agency to give the Ombudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers necessary, being information:  (i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the member has access; and  (ii) that is relevant to the inspection." ;
    skos:definition "(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this section, the Ombudsman:  (a) after notifying the chief officer of the agency, may enter at any reasonable time premises occupied by the agency; and  (b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times to all records of the agency that are relevant to the inspection; and  (c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to take extracts from, records of the agency; and  (d) may require a member of staff of the agency to give the Ombudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers necessary, being information:  (i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the member has access; and  (ii) that is relevant to the inspection."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a7f4c13f9abc28e3a2675eb1eb1d2094985fe011c0675f9afa95a58b104e3880" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186b ;
    cof:pageNumber "421"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Ombudsman may enter premises, access records, and require staff information." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.421" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186b-ss-2-norm .
