    skos:definition "(3) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law, prevents an officer of an enforcement agency from:  (a) giving information to an inspecting officer (whether orally or in writing and whether or not in answer to a question); or  (b) giving access to a record of the agency to an inspecting officer; for the purposes of an inspection under this Chapter of the agency’s records.  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Chapter 4A  Section 186E  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
